{"v":"3.0.0","project":{"accession":"PRJNA1280557","title":"16S rRNA sequencing data of intestinal flora","description":"The aim of this study was to determine the effects of repeated sevoflurane (Sev) exposure and the possible role of gut-brain axis. Thirty 28-day Sprague-Dawley rats were randomly divided into five experimental groups.The Sev group was exposed to 3.2 % sevoflurane for 2 h on postnatal day (P) 35, P42, and P49. The Sev-Con group only received carrier gas for 2 h at the same time points. The ANT group received antibiotic pre-treatment only since P28 for 3 weeks. The Sev+ANT group was treated with antibiotics for 3 weeks and then exposed to 3.2% sevoflurane for 2 h at each time point. Control group (Con group): animals were freely raised without special treatment.Finally, the 16S rRNA sequencing indicated that at the genus level, Ligilactobacillus, Faecousia, and Alloprevotella showed an increasing trend, while Lactobacillus showed a decreasing trend. The results may reflect that multiple exposures to Sev anesthesia may induce or aggravate cognitive impairment through the gut-brain axis at the developmental stage.","organism":null,"data_type":"Raw sequence reads","center_name":"Affiliated Hospital of Zunyi Medical University","submission_date":"2025/06/22 00:00","last_update":null},"sample_cols":["accession","title","collection_date","country","region","city","lat","lon","urban_status","urban_context","eligibility_reason","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","host","location_resolution","country_iso2","place_id","location_status","location_method","location_note","geo_loc_raw","collection_year"],"samples":[["SAMN49527042","Metagenome or environmental sample from activated sludge metagenome","2023-11-02","China","Guizhou",null,null,null,"uncertain",null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical",null,null,null,null,null,"region","CN",null,"unresolved",null,null,"China:Guizhou",2023],["SAMN49527043","Metagenom